# Django Backend Architecture Rules - Arcanovi Project

## Core Principles

**Feature-Driven Design (FDD)**: Each Django app represents one feature domain with complete aspect-based separation following the EXACT directory structure: `backend/api/apps/{featurename}/` with all subdirectories as specified.

**Clean Architecture**: Maintain strict layering - Domain Models → Service Layer → API Layer → Interface Layer using the prescribed naming conventions without underscores.

**Domain Isolation**: Features communicate only through well-defined interfaces, events, or service calls - never direct model imports between features.

## Feature Structure Standards

### Directory Organization (MANDATORY)
```
backend/api/apps/{featurename}/
├── models/                     # Domain Models (aspektbasiert)
│   ├── model{aspect1}.py      # z.B. modeluser.py
│   ├── model{aspect2}.py      # z.B. modelorganization.py
│   ├── model{aspect3}.py      # z.B. modelteam.py
│   └── __init__.py            # Zentraler Export aller Models
├── services/                   # Business Logic & CRUD Operations
│   ├── crud{aspect1}.py       # z.B. cruduser.py
│   ├── crud{aspect2}.py       # z.B. crudorganization.py
│   └── crud{aspect3}.py       # z.B. crudteam.py
├── api/                       # REST API Layer
│   ├── endpoints/             # View-Funktionen (aspektbasiert)
│   │   ├── view{aspect1}.py   # z.B. viewuser.py
│   │   ├── view{aspect2}.py   # z.B. vieworganization.py
│   │   └── view{aspect3}.py   # z.B. viewteam.py
│   ├── serializers/           # DRF Serializers (aspektbasiert)
│   │   ├── serializer{aspect1}.py
│   │   ├── serializer{aspect2}.py
│   │   └── serializer{aspect3}.py
│   └── urls/                  # URL-Konfiguration (aspektbasiert)
│       ├── urls{aspect1}.py
│       ├── urls{aspect2}.py
│       └── urls{aspect3}.py
├── listeners/                 # Event Handling & Background Tasks
│   ├── crud{aspect1}.py       # Django Signals für CRUD-Events
│   ├── crud{aspect2}.py
│   ├── streaming{aspect1}.py  # SSE-Events (optional)
│   ├── tasks{aspect1}.py      # Background Tasks (optional)
│   └── __init__.py
├── tests/                     # Test Suite (aspektbasiert)
│   ├── models/                # Model Tests
│   │   ├── test{aspect1}models.py
│   │   └── test{aspect2}models.py
│   ├── api/                   # API Tests
│   │   ├── test{aspect1}api.py
│   │   └── test{aspect2}api.py
│   ├── services/              # Service Tests
│   │   ├── test{aspect1}services.py
│   │   └── test{aspect2}services.py
│   └── __init__.py
├── migrations/                # Django Database Migrations
├── sql/                       # Custom SQL Scripts (optional)
├── management/                # Django Management Commands
│   └── commands/
├── apps.py                    # Django App Configuration
├── urls.py                    # Haupt-URL-Konfiguration
└── README.md                  # Feature-Dokumentation
```

### Aspect-Based File Naming (EXACT CONVENTIONS)
- Models: `model{aspect}.py` (z.B. `modeluser.py`, `modelorganization.py`)
- Services: `crud{aspect}.py` (z.B. `cruduser.py`, `crudteam.py`)
- Views: `view{aspect}.py` (z.B. `viewuser.py`, `viewauthentication.py`)
- Serializers: `serializer{aspect}.py`
- URLs: `urls{aspect}.py`
- Tests: `test{aspect}{layer}.py` (z.B. `testusermodels.py`, `testuserapi.py`)

## Implementation Guidelines

### Models Layer
- Every model MUST have an `entity_id` field with pattern `{prefix}-{12_digit_id}`
- Explicit `db_table` definitions following convention: `{feature_prefix}_{aspect}_{entity}`
- Centralized model exports in `models/__init__.py`
- Abstract base models in shared/core app for common patterns
- No business logic in models - keep them as data containers

### Services Layer
- Static methods for all CRUD operations with clear separation of concerns
- Comprehensive error handling with proper logging
- Database transactions for critical operations
- Type hints for all parameters and return values
- Services are framework-agnostic - no Django request objects as parameters
- Services communicate between features through well-defined interfaces

### API Layer
- Function-based views with explicit decorators for permissions and authentication
- Separate serializers for input validation and output formatting
- Consistent error response format across all endpoints
- JWT authentication integration with proper token validation
- CORS configuration for React frontend integration
- SSE endpoints for real-time streaming with proper connection management (optional)

### Event Handling
- Django signals for CRUD events with audit logging
- Background tasks using Django's built-in mechanisms or lightweight alternatives
- SSE streaming for real-time updates (optional, when applicable)
- Event-driven communication between features to maintain loose coupling

### Testing Requirements
- Minimum 80% code coverage
- Separate test files for each layer (models, services, api)
- Integration tests for complete workflows
- API tests using Django REST framework test client
- Mock external dependencies
- Test SSE connections and streaming functionality (if implemented)

## Security & Performance

### Authentication & Authorization
- JWT-based authentication for all protected endpoints
- Role-based access control (RBAC) using Django groups and permissions
- Permission classes for fine-grained access control
- No hardcoded permissions in views - use centralized permission system

### Database Optimization
- Use `select_related()` and `prefetch_related()` for efficient queries
- Database indexing on frequently filtered fields
- Pagination for all list endpoints
- Bulk operations for large data sets

### Caching Strategy
- Database-based caching for session management and frequent queries
- Cache invalidation on model updates using Django's cache framework
- Proper cache key naming conventions
- No Redis dependency - use Django's database cache backend

## Error Handling & Logging

### Logging Standards
- Structured logging with appropriate levels (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR)
- Log all critical operations with entity_ids for traceability
- Separate log files for different components
- No sensitive data in logs

### Error Management
- Consistent error response format
- Proper exception handling in all layers
- Client-friendly error messages
- Server error tracking and monitoring integration

## Development Workflow

### Code Quality
- Type hints for all public methods
- Comprehensive docstrings following Django conventions
- Consistent code formatting (Black, flake8)
- Regular dependency updates with security checks

### Migration Management
- Descriptive migration names
- Data migrations separate from schema migrations
- Backup strategies for production migrations
- Migration testing in staging environment

### Documentation
- Feature README with usage examples
- API documentation with endpoint specifications
- Architecture decision records for major design choices
- Deployment and configuration guides

## Background Task Processing

### Without Redis/Celery
- Use Django's `django.core.management.commands` for scheduled tasks
- Database-based task queuing for asynchronous operations
- Consider lightweight alternatives like `django-q` or `django-background-tasks`
- Simple cron jobs for periodic tasks
- Proper error handling and retry mechanisms